---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro";
import AgentIcon from "./AgentIcon.astro";
import { leaders, leadersReadOn, mixing } from "../data/leaders";

// Figs. 3 and 4. Identity, not magnitude, is the finding: a different agent
// leads each row. Scores sit on different scales, so they stay as numbers in
// their own units, not bars on one axis.
---
<div class="leaders">
<figure data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
  <ol class="leader-list" role="list">
    {leaders.map((row) => (
      <li class="leader">
        <span class="label leader-capability">{row.capability}</span>
        <span class="leader-name">
          <AgentIcon name={row.through} size={14} />
          <strong>{row.leader}</strong>
          <span class="leader-through">in {row.throughLabel}</span>
        </span>
        <span class="leader-value">{row.value}{row.unit && <span class="leader-unit"> {row.unit}</span>}</span>
        <span class="leader-detail">
          {row.detail}
          {row.sources.map((source) => <a class="text-link" href={source.href}>{source.label}<Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={12} /></a>)}
        </span>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    <span class="caption-title"><span class="caption-number">Fig. 3</span>Who leads each kind of work, read {leadersReadOn}</span>
    <span class="caption-note">Values as each source reports them. Scores use different scales, so compare within a row, not across rows.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<figure data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 120ms" class="mixing">
    <ul role="list">
      {mixing.map((item) => (
        <li>
          <span class="label">{item.stance}</span>
          <span>{item.finding} <a class="text-link" href={item.source.href}>{item.source.label}<Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={12} /></a></span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="mixing-lesson">A team helps when each member brings something the others lack, and when the answer is picked well. So Ennodia routes each part to the agent with the ability, and Compare stays optional.</p>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    <span class="caption-title"><span class="caption-number">Fig. 4</span>Does combining answers help? One finding for, one against</span>
    <span class="caption-note">From each paper’s abstract.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
